{"tag":"F5X3","kind":"problem","subkind":"problem","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"problem-1","file":"","label":"pr1","number":"1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Problem","body_md":"\\label{pr1}\n \tIs the Chein automorphism (\\ref{f2}) of the free metabelian algebra Lie algebra $M_n$ of rank $n\\geq 4$ tame?","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"problem","item":"problem","head":"environment","counter":"problem","number_from":"render","labels":["pr1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":139,"to":141},"hash":"sha256:709fa2127aadbd31c30ba390b8ad38f55d7086899cdd9b7ff636d17443652cb7","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"KZYM","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-1","file":"","label":"l1","number":"1","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l1}\n$(a)$ The group of tame $\\mathrm{IA}$-automorphisms $\\mathrm{TAut}(M_n)\\cap \\mathrm{IAut}(M_n)$ is generated by all linear conjugates of elementary automorphisms of the form (\\ref{f5}) where $f\\in M_n'$ does not depend on $x_1$;\n\n$(b)$ The group almost tame $\\mathrm{IA}$-automorphisms  $\\mathrm{ATAut}(M_n)\\cap \\mathrm{IAut}(M_n)$ is generated by all linear conjugates of Chein automorphisms of the form (\\ref{f5}).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":252,"to":256},"hash":"sha256:bf049df3493ba73cde27a7aa6dcc80c89d8292e14a5bfb7965ad8af25fe6cda0","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"CVJL","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-2","file":"","label":"l2","number":"2","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l2} \\cite[Lemma 1]{AutoI} Let $a=(a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n)^t\\in (U^n)^t$ be an arbitrary column of dimension $n$ over $U$. \nThen the following conditions are equivalent. \n\n$(1)$ $a=\\partial(f)$ for some $f\\in M_n'$; \n\n$(2)$  $Ya=y_1a_1+\\ldots +y_na_n=0$ where $Y=(y_1,\\ldots,y_n)$; \n\n$(3)$ $a=\\sum_{i\u003cj} (e_iy_j-e_jy_i)a_{ij}, \\ a_{ij}\\in U$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":329,"to":337},"hash":"sha256:55cd52a356e81c6c726d99a2ffd1bcb3950234f763a050bc9e76373a8260b511","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"C1JB","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-3","file":"","label":"l3","number":"3","section":"sec-2","order":4,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l3} \\cite[Lemma 2]{AutoI}\nAn endomorphism $\\phi$ of $M_n$ is an automorphism if and only if the Jacobian matrix $J(\\phi)$ is invertible.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":357,"to":359},"hash":"sha256:2f0b3d7596d4aada44df40cbc0b1d41ab8dda3fba81460aafae265c9ee8e391a","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"4QJR","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-4","file":"","label":"l4","number":"4","section":"sec-2","order":5,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l4} \\cite[Lemma 3]{AutoI} An endomorphism of $M_n$ of the form (\\ref{f5}) \n is an automorphism if and only if $f$ belongs to the ideal generated by all $[x_s,x_t]$, where $s,t\\neq 1$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l4"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":364,"to":366},"hash":"sha256:78bf1bdf6c785f79f7beb973c130d9619b999bcdc5cc0765b69d946f4e5f5988","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"ECD6","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-5","file":"","label":"l5","number":"5","section":"sec-2","order":6,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l5} $(a)$ If $\\phi, \\psi\\in  \\mathrm{IAut}(M_n)$ then \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nJ(\\phi\\psi)=J(\\phi) J(\\psi); \n\\end{eqnarray*}\n\n$(b)$  If $\\phi\\in  \\mathrm{IAut}(M_n)$ and $\\alpha\\in GL_n(K)$ then \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nJ(\\alpha \\phi \\alpha^{-1})=\\alpha J(\\phi)^{\\alpha} \\alpha^{-1}; \n\\end{eqnarray*}\n\n$(c)$ \n The map \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nJ : \\mathrm{IAut}(M_n) \\to SL_n(U)\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nis an injective homomorphism of groups and $G=J(\\mathrm{IAut}(M_n))$ is the set of all matrics from  $SL_n(U)$ of the form \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nI+A, \n\\end{eqnarray*}\nwhere $A\\in \\mathrm{Mat}_n(U)$ is a matrix such that $YA=0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l5"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":380,"to":400},"hash":"sha256:56dbfabad84f1dfcfd9fedddf4148ef161e84cc516eda3f9da14c20af610d3c6","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"RCYB","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-6","file":"","label":"l6","number":"6","section":"sec-3","order":7,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l6} $(a)$ \nThe group $T$ is generated by all linear conjugates of matrices of the form (\\ref{f7}) where $a$ does not depend on $y_1$. \n\n$(b)$ The group $S$ is generated by all linear conjugates of matrices of the form (\\ref{f7}).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l6"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":524,"to":528},"hash":"sha256:fdd7137e858b66ceb7b26ba9a79476fbbcde67936ef3fea3a921ce91fcfe72d5","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"TIH4","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-1","file":"","label":"p1","number":"1","section":"sec-3","order":8,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p1} Let $n\\geq 4$ and $K$ is a field of characteristic $\\neq 3$ or $n\\geq 5$. \n\t\n\t$(1)$ Every matrix of the form (\\ref{f7}) belongs to $T$ if $\\mathrm{ldeg}(a)\\geq 2$; \n\t\n\t$(2)$ Every matrix of the form \n\t\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\tI+ay_1F_{121}+ay_2F_{122}\n\t\\end{eqnarray*}\n\tbelongs to $T$ if $\\mathrm{ldeg}(a)\\geq 2$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":540,"to":549},"hash":"sha256:cebafc795b279a22be0428814620a3f826cfed665413cab584b7bbc6f4894d70","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"3ST2","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"corollary-1","file":"","label":"c0","number":"1","section":"sec-3","order":9,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{c0} \\cite[Corollary 1]{AutoI} Let $n\\geq 4$ and $K$ is a field of characteristic $\\neq 3$ or $n\\geq 5$.\n\tThe group of all almost tame automorphisms $\\mathrm{ATAut}(M_n)$ is generated, modulo all linear automorphisms, by the quadratic automorphism (\\ref{f1}) and the  cubic automorphism (\\ref{f2}).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","labels":["c0"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":560,"to":562},"hash":"sha256:79ba110ddf6e7d1b29d45984ce24f44d671a9f3c27573b1c6de643edc9ab7c2f","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"ZMF9","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-2","file":"","label":"p2","number":"2","section":"sec-3","order":10,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p2} Every matrix of the form \n\t\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\tI+ay_1F_{121}+ay_2F_{122}\n\t\\end{eqnarray*}\n\twith $\\mathrm{ldeg}(a)\\geq 1$ belongs to $S$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":565,"to":570},"hash":"sha256:643a2afda8bd7711daa6be33f485fa37396a9a64bff0176ffada648476c2401d","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-10","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"MAEV","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-7","file":"","label":"l9","number":"7","section":"sec-4","order":11,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l9}\nLet $B$ be any matrix from $SL_{n-1}(U,y_nU)$. Then $B=I_{n-1}+y_nC$ for some matrix $C\\in \\mathrm{Mat}_{n-1}(U)$ and there exists a unique special matrix $Z$ such that \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nZ=I+\\left[\\begin{array}{cc}\n y_nC  \u0026 0  \\\\\n *  \u0026  0  \\\\\n \\end{array}\\right].\n\\end{eqnarray*}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l9"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":619,"to":627},"hash":"sha256:a1346ca94997dc8a2e4b3a908233951022c1c88735915315ef84e4de1cf52af8","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"LL7X","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-3","file":"","label":"p3","number":"3","section":"sec-4","order":12,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p3} Every matrix of the form   \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nA(h,f,g)=I +hfgF_{1n1}+hg^2F_{2n1}-hf^2F_{1n2}-hfgF_{2n2}\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nbelongs to $S$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":659,"to":664},"hash":"sha256:ad12cbd15577f1429fdaabd41ba357e76f1d8391262ee126b3df88053f87836f","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-12","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"XQQZ","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-4","file":"","label":"p4","number":"4","section":"sec-4","order":13,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p4}\nLet  $k\\geq 3$ and $J=y_nU$. Then \n\n(1) $SL_k(U,J)=E_k(U,J)$;\n\n(2) $E_k(U,J)$  is generated by the set of all matrices of the form \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nI_k+h(fe_i+ge_j)(ge_i-fe_j)^t=I_k+hfg(E_{ii}-E_{jj})+hg^2E_{ji}-hf^2E_{ij}\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nwhere $i\u003cj$, $h\\in J$, and $f,g\\in U$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p4"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":708,"to":718},"hash":"sha256:345e71b44aafdd1a6581279f56f05dae5aafe9a719afe276679630d3343cb936","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-13","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"2JD7","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-5","file":"","label":"p5","number":"5","section":"sec-4","order":14,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p5} \nEvery special matrix belongs to $S$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p5"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":765,"to":767},"hash":"sha256:eeea0fd1de41978679c63b696a4d442a99dc628d22b0b0d80df55ba3894b1744","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-14","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"H5JJ","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"corollary-2","file":"","label":"c9","number":"2","section":"sec-4","order":15,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{c9}\nEvery automorphism of the form \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\n(x_1+f_1,x_2+f_2,\\ldots,x_{n-1}+f_{n-1}, x_n), \n\\end{eqnarray*}\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_{n-1}$ belong to the ideal generated by $[x_1,x_n],\\ldots,[x_{n-1},x_n]$, is almost tame.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","labels":["c9"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":785,"to":791},"hash":"sha256:ef6d2f6b5bf8c461f07757047995439c62b2b5a34a1cac378a4d4ed154b59bd0","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-15","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"GYFM","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-8","file":"","label":"l15","number":"8","section":"sec-5","order":16,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l15}\nLet $B=I+[a_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^ny_pU)\\cap G$ be such that   \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\na_{in}\\in\n\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU+y_n^2U\n\\end{eqnarray*}\n and  \n \\begin{eqnarray*}\n \\mathrm{ldeg}(\\overline{a}_{in})\\geq 3\n \\end{eqnarray*}\n  for all $1\\leq i\\leq n-1$, where $\\overline{a}_{in}$ is obtained from $a_{in}$ by setting $y_s=y_{s+1}=\\ldots =y_{n-1}=0$. Then there exists $C\\in S$ such that $C^{-1}B\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l15"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":818,"to":829},"hash":"sha256:c953a7987e9bc7336b93a20724b558d8551779d2db6b058f205e663181478cff","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-16","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"YPL6","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-9","file":"","label":"l91","number":"9","section":"sec-6","order":17,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l91}\nThe automorphism \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\tau=(x_1+[[x_1,x_2],x_1],x_2+[[x_1,x_2],x_2],x_3,\\ldots,x_n)\n\\end{eqnarray*} is almost tame.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l91"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1133,"to":1138},"hash":"sha256:1624aec68213c842abe2eaea3d8a5a054a3caec1df6242c37eaeea480e4770c2","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-17","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"DWA7","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"corollary-3","file":"","label":"c2","number":"3","section":"sec-6","order":18,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{c2}\nThe matrix (\\ref{f9}) belongs to $S$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","labels":["c2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1224,"to":1226},"hash":"sha256:5546b63ef44219dd014510fe86ee677654c7b5a03b1ff27ed548700af86138c9","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-18","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"5T3M","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-10","file":"","label":"l12","number":"10","section":"sec-7","order":19,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l12} There exists a $3$-reducible matrix $C$ in $T$ such that $C_3$ after setting $y_2=y_3=0$ becomes equal to \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nI_3+\\lambda y_1E_{31}=I_3+\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n0 \u0026 0 \u0026 0\\\\\n0 \u0026 0 \u0026 0\\\\\n\\lambda y_1 \u0026 0 \u0026 0\n\\end{bmatrix},\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nwhere $\\lambda\\in K$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l12"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1247,"to":1257},"hash":"sha256:6d2f4011c16110749c4d64e5d535c5ff42d8e1bcc23eadb59b171cc14b8b4444","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-19","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"DTZF","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-11","file":"","label":"l13","number":"11","section":"sec-7","order":20,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l13} Let \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nI_n+[a_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,y_1U+y_2U)\\cap G.\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nThen $\\mathrm{ldeg}(a_{ij})\\geq 2$ for all $1\\leq i,j\\leq 2$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l13"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1296,"to":1301},"hash":"sha256:71de259eb036d17c2af29984f03cb1d43ca6b390bdc20a007307458191a94c10","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-20","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"KRPY","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-12","file":"","label":"l14","number":"12","section":"sec-7","order":21,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l14} Let \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nA=I_n+[a_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^ny_pU)\\cap G.\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nThen there exists $R\\in S$ such that  $R^{-1}A=I_n+[e_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^ny_pU)\\cap G$\n and $e_{1n},e_{2n}, \\ldots, e_{n-1 n}\\in\n\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU+y_n^2U$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l14"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1340,"to":1347},"hash":"sha256:775ee89546db9bea664f1c41dd785e3b97719688544295e0c1f365bc59583bd4","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-21","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"P7B4","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"lemma-13","file":"","label":"l","number":"13","section":"sec-7","order":22,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l}\nLet $A=I_n+[a_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^ny_pU)\\cap G$ and  \n$a_{1n},a_{2n}, \\ldots, a_{(n-1) n}\\in\n\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU+y_n^2U$. Then there exists $B\\in S$ such that $B^{-1}A\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"lemma","number_from":"render","labels":["l"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1518,"to":1522},"hash":"sha256:03f46cf4485b8df2a28e2167d65d517adf27c894826f5ad854261bf72516fced","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-22","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"9GR1","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"proposition-6","file":"","label":"p6","number":"6","section":"sec-7","order":23,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{p6} Let \n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nA=I+[a_{ij}]\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^ny_pU)\\cap G.\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nThen there exists $B\\in S$ such that $B^{-1}A\\in SL_n(U,\\sum_{p=s}^{n-1}y_pU)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["p6"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1535,"to":1540},"hash":"sha256:e8e379d2a790ba30b61e5b2baaa44250e3e7f0527e683228d547b225cb577207","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-23","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"3S78","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"theorem-1","file":"","label":"t1","number":"1","section":"sec-8","order":24,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{t1}\nEvery automorphism of the free metabelian Lie algebra $M_n$ of rank $n\\geq 4$ over an arbitrary field $K$ is almost tame.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["t1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1553,"to":1555},"hash":"sha256:2aaba3a0d4f5416a2ca6e44aea0e03d8d5a572f00213105c5d24565264fdaaae","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-24","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"V4M1","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"theorem-2","file":"","label":"t2","number":"2","section":"sec-8","order":25,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{t2} The automorphism group $\\mathrm{Aut}(M_n)$ of the free metabelian Lie algebra $M_n$ of rank $n\\geq 4$ over a field $K$ of characteristic different from $3$ is generated by its linear automorphisms together with the quadratic automorphism (\\ref{f1}) and the cubic automorphism (\\ref{f2}).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["t2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1581,"to":1582},"hash":"sha256:519c1830e4cf6f6eda489afced74e9e7076e73e4ec30be548c4669a3769f5a29","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-25","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
{"tag":"VA0C","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.21954","version":"1","local":"corollary-4","file":"","label":"c3","number":"4","section":"sec-8","order":26,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{c3} The automorphism group $\\mathrm{Aut}(M_n)$ of the free metabelian Lie algebra $M_n$ of rank $n\\geq 5$ over a field $K$  is generated by its linear automorphisms together with the quadratic automorphism (\\ref{f1}) and the cubic automorphism (\\ref{f2}).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"corollary","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"corollary","number_from":"render","labels":["c3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Auto_Met_II.tex","from":1585,"to":1586},"hash":"sha256:d3ca95c394f3371004307c89f8c8a36cca23be7556dfda0d4d1184087ec0115e","minhash":"","census":"2610.21954v1#env-26","extractor":"ax/v0.5.24"}
